{"duration_api_ms":126222,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"309c3ed7-f371-40b9-893d-ee8f708b6828","total_cost_usd":0.7144478000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40098,"cache_read_input_tokens":774299,"output_tokens":11935,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1675},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40098,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1131,"cache_read_input_tokens":71932,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":504},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":11935,"cacheReadInputTokens":774299,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40098,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7144478000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1675,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":40098,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I mapped the `open-docx-real-internet` journey and committed the work. Opening the real 11-page docx on the emulated 50/10 Mbps, 30 ms link takes **6 601 ms** (p50 of 5 runs, range 6 580–6 895). That is 1 627 ms more than the 4 974 ms the same journey took without throttling in PKT-0135. All acceptance commands pass, `theseus validate` reports 0 errors, and `theseus scope-check` reports no files outside the target.\n\n- **Measurement:** `serve-integrated.sh` already existed, so I reused it. I added `open-docx-real-internet.sh` and its runner, a copy of the `open-docx-real` runner that turns on Chrome's network emulation. The upload now goes through the page itself, so it pays the 10 Mbps uplink like a real user. Every download is assigned to the module that asks for it, by URL.\n- **The map:** `.theseus/journeys/open-docx-real-internet.md` has 12 stages that add up exactly to 6 601 ms, with nothing unattributed. By module:\n\n| Module | ms | Share |\n|---|---|---|\n| project | 3 477 | 52.7 % |\n| web-apps-documenteditor | 1 228 | 18.6 % |\n| sdkjs-word | 1 118 | 16.9 % |\n| sdkjs-common | 373 | 5.7 % |\n| x2t | 267 | 4.0 % |\n| docservice | 138 | 2.1 % |\n\n- **Biggest cost:** uploading the 2.8 MB file takes 2 785 ms, 42 % of the total. It went from 75 ms to 2 785 ms and accounts for almost all of the extra time over the unthrottled run.\n- **How I split the client time:** as in PKT-0135, the 1 594 ms between receiving the converted document and the editor reporting it loaded is split using the CPU shares profiled in PKT-0043. It is an estimate, not a profile of this sample. The conversion time (267 ms) comes from the converter log.\n\n**Surprises:**\n- The example's landing page has a preloader that starts downloading about 2.9 MB of editor code 16 ms after the user picks the file, while the upload is still going. So on a real link most of that download hides behind the upload. After the document starts loading, the time is about the same as unthrottled (2 696 vs 2 465 ms).\n- The emulation reports 0 bytes for the converted document (`Editor.bin`) and the 7 images, and `Editor.bin` arrives in 15 ms. They are probably not being throttled, so that stage is probably too low, by roughly 100–200 ms (my estimate). I didn't confirm the cause. I recorded a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/` to find out, which needs the `documentserver` and `browser` environments.\n\nThe executor log and my friction line are written. My first friction line used the wrong format and failed `validate`, so I rewrote it.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Throttled journeys must send the upload through the page's own network requests; the request helper used before skips the emulated link.\n- Check the reported byte counts for each download: the emulation does not see some responses, and nothing warns you.\n- The example's preloader is part of what a user actually goes through on a real link.","ttft_ms":3121,"type":"result","duration_ms":241958,"uuid":"93bb3358-f44c-40e4-b6e2-0b0ec80a81dc","ttft_stream_ms":1964,"time_to_request_ms":420,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":283,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":21,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":41,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":179,"time_to_request_major_faults":16,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":243,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4023,"process_wall_ms_turn":241957,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1638,"process_wall_ms_streaming":98153,"main_stream_count":13,"main_stream_event_count":1700,"main_stream_chunk_count":1373,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1638,"wall_ms":98153,"entries":13},"tool":{"cpu_ms":1429,"wall_ms":115138,"entries":12},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":520,"wall_ms":28010,"entries":13},"before_